before`). The `parses` guard is always declared and makes NO CLAIM for a path without a parser (markdown, shell). Floor of CART-1182: text on the graph's own world; term kinds, namespace addresses and non-disk commits are next |\n| Rename a record's FIELD (not a name): its reads and the constructors that define it, with an occupied target asked, not refused | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/toolbelt.lua run rename-field <root> base=<spelling> field=<old> to=<new> define=<a.lua,b.lua> [accept=name-occupied] [apply=1]`; in a tactic `T.step('rename-field', { base, field, to, define })`. Reads = `<base>.<field>` (rooted by SPELLING — `spec.scopes`, never `L.scopes`; a record read under another name is the frontier); keys = `field =` in the define files (omitted: a DECISION listing every file with such a key). An OCCUPIED target (a read or a key already named `to`) is a `name-occupied` DECISION; accepted, the occupant moves to the placeholder `<to>__1` in the same plan and a `placeholder` residue says to choose its real name (CART-1009). Comment/string mentions: a counted `text-mentions` frontier, never rewritten. Replayed on CART-1160 step 7 (2203d17^): the same 3 reads + 3 keys, `binders` stopped as occupied. CART-1175 |\n| Deploy through a PLAN with review gates and a real undo (release, switch, health check; roll back on failure) | `nvim --headless -u NONE -l tools/toolbelt.lua run deploy <root> from=<src dir> target=<deploy dir> [approve=yes] [rollback=1] [apply=1]` — the local deployment world (cartograph.deploy): `release` writes releases/<content id>/ (an immutable VALUE; a cross-world create journaled in the target's journal; the same content is the same id, so a re-release is empty), `switch` moves CURRENT (COMPENSABLE: its recorded inverse switches back, CART-1186; gated by the `approve-deploy` DECISION), then the `deploy-health` PREMISE (automated review). Gates: `target-write` + `approve-deploy` (approve=yes, or a remembered decision). rollback=1: a failed