text}, {'supplied-text'})), { apply = true, oracle = fn })` → `status` done / previewed / stopped (a decision, with `options` + `fixes`) / failed (class, where); `residue`, `work_orders` (every unbuilt stop), `rolled_back`. A DRY run (`apply = false`, the default) CHAINS OVERLAY WORLDS: each journaled step's staged texts become a virtual graph (`world.edit`) the next step plans in, so the whole term previews — `preview` = { [rel] = final text }, `worlds` = how many were stacked, the caller's graph comes back afterwards; a dry `repeat` converges on its own effect; a failed dry alternative drops its world; after a non-journaled step the rest is `underivable` (CART-1160 step 3). FORWARD RECOVERY: a run that stops KEEPS its completed steps (`completed`, each with its `effect`) and resuming is RE-RUNNING the same term with the decision answered in the step's `accept` list — every verb is goal-checked, so a completed step is `empty` the second time (`resumable`); `on_stop = 'rollback'` undoes a stopped run only over journaled writes. Verbs declare `effect` (journaled / compensable / irreversible; undeclared = irreversible, never inside first/try/repeat) and `rerun = 'empty'`. Verbs: `compose.VERBS` (moveset, replace, annotate, clonemerge), addressed by durable ref. One step alone: `tactic.step(store, {verb, args, accept}, {apply})` (compose's recipes run on it). CART-1152 |\n| Did you mean? — correct a refused invocation's argument (a slipped name, a wrong file, a symbol that MOVED or was RENAMED) | in a tactic: a plan-phase `ill-posed`/`stale` refusal asks `require('cartograph.correct').suggest(store, spec, args)` (the adapter declares `correct = { ref = 'ref' }` / `{ seed_refs = 'refs' }`) and keeps the candidates the VERB accepts (a dry step, no failing guard). ★ AUTOMATIC ONLY ON PROVENANCE: a stale ref to a symbol THIS run's own step moved (the adapter's `provides`; also on a resume, where the move is empty) is corrected, and listed in `result.corrections`. Everything INFERRED (edit distance, the witness — a SHAPE hash, CART-1154 —, the same name elsewhere, a same-shaped rename) is a DECISION whose options carry the corrected args (`source` moved|near|renamed|elsewhere, `CONTRADICTS` when the ref's witness disagrees). A witnessed ref whose symbol is GONE fails `stale` and lists near names for information. `opts.correct = 'ask' | 'off'`. Edit distance: `require('cartograph.near').within(key, set)` (all candidates, ties kept) |\n| Why did a write verb STOP, and what should a tactic do next? (the stop CLASS: decision / unbuilt / frontier / ill-posed / stale / empty / informational / environment) | a refusal's third return (`local plan, why, class = verb.plan(…)`; before the write, `txn.stage(store, plan)` — the ONE staging preview and apply share — answers `nil, why, class`; optapply-family CODES map via `require('cartograph.hazard').CODE_CLASS`); a hazard row's `.class`; on the wire `refusal.class` and the hazards note's `evidence.hazards[i].class` (`hazard.plain(list)` is the JSON-safe form — a raw row encodes as `[]`). Vocabulary: `hazard.CLASSES`; fenced by `tests/stopclass_spec.lua` (CART-1152) |\n| Read a metaprogram's sites: what a site of a declared shape GENERATES, with the site on every fact | `require('cartograph.generators').read(gen, troot, src, file)` → facts, refusals (shape / hole / context), selected; declarations: `spec.<lang>.generators`, `packs.rails.generators`, `generators.from_erlreg(erlreg.CARRIERS)`; a form is a SOURCE SNIPPET with `__hole` / `__rest__` placeholders (`generators.snippet(A, lang, text, holes, wrap)`), an output a text template (`'$owner#$assoc='`), the site selector derived from the forms |\n| What can a dynamic erlang `Mod:f(...)` run? | the `erldispatch` post-pass (`require('cartograph.erldispatch').attach(data)`, in `postpass.PASSES`): hedged `dyn` edges to the implementers of the behaviour that declares f/n as a -callback (own / single / several = union marked `pop_ambiguous` / none), the -callback as `pop`; stats and rows in `data.erldispatch`. ejabberd: 436 of 582 dynamic calls get a population, 1553 edges, 1034 functions whose only in-tree caller is a dispatch edge |\n| What runs when a hook fires? Which hooks are run but registered nowhere (the plugin surface), which registered but never run? | the `erlhooks` post-pass (`require('cartograph.erlhooks').attach(data)` → `data.erlhooks`: `.unregistered`, `.unrun`, `.verbs`): hedged `ref` edges tagged `hook = key` from every dispatch site to the handlers registered under its key; registrations from the derived interpreter's tuples and direct calls, dispatch verbs = calls into the registry module that INVOKE (dynamic call / apply). ejabberd: 530 registrations, 257 dispatch sites, 750 edges, 55 hooks run with no registration, 372 handlers reachable only through a hook |\n| Which handle_call/handle_cast clause does a gen_server message reach — and which gen_statem clause (handle_event/4, or the state functions)? Which specific clauses does nothing in the tree send to? | the `erlmsg` post-pass (`require('cartograph.erlmsg').attach(data)` → `data.erlmsg`: `.rows`, `.unreached`; `erlmsg.unify(p, ps, v, vs)` three-valued): hedged `ref` edges tagged `msg = call|cast`, `clauses = {lines}`; the server explicit (?MODULE, a module atom, or built from one through a binding / single-clause helper / same-file macro) or chosen by the message among SPECIFIC clauses. gen_statem by callback mode (handle_event_function: handle_event/4 with the event type admitted; state_functions: every state function, gen_statem's own arity-3 callbacks excluded from the otp-api profile). ejabberd: 120 sites (24 gen_statem), 118 reach a clause, 92 edges, 16 specific clauses unreached |\n| Which definition does a same-file call reach when the preprocessor picks one per build? | the `erlvariants` post-pass (`require('cartograph.erlvariants').attach(data)`): a `samefile` refusal whose candidates sit in mutually exclusive -ifdef/-ifndef/-